Package: irrd-ng
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Josh Finlay <josh@athenanetworks.com.au>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: adduser
Recommends: unattended-upgrades
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/JoshFinlayAU/irrd-ng
Description: Internet Routing Registry daemon, drop-in replacement for IRRd 4.5
 irrd-ng is a drop-in replacement for IRRd 4.5, the Internet Routing
 Registry daemon, written in Rust. It reads the same irrd.yaml, answers
 whois and HTTP queries byte for byte as IRRd 4.5.4 does, serves and
 mirrors NRTM, and installs the same command line tools (irrd, irrdctl,
 irrd_load_database and the rest), all from one static binary with an
 embedded store. It needs no PostgreSQL, Redis or Python.
 .
 Moving from IRRd v4 takes a one-shot import of the v4 database. The
 package does not start irrd-ng while IRRd v4 is running or before the
 import; run "irrd-ng migrate-check" for the steps that remain.
 .
 The package also adds the irrd-ng APT repository, so that
 unattended-upgrades keeps irrd-ng up to date.
